# Setup PIP enviornment
`pip install -e .`

# Bot
the library in src/bot is the primary entry point for users of this SDK, this contains a wrapper around the openapi_client with some convienence methods.

# Available Executable CLI tools
the enviornment includes the folowing executable scripts to help interact with the game server.
these CLI tools all contain a --help option that prints information about how to use them.

### `poker-tui`
a textual user interface that can be used to view/play a game from the perspective of a player

### `new-game`
creates a game on the server

### `join-game`
join a created game with a set of users

### `start-game`
start a created game - locking the ability to join and begining play

### `get-game`
get the state of a running game

### `listen-game`
attach a listener to a running game that echos websocket messages to stdout

# Tests
the tests in test/ all have side effects in that they create games on the server.
these are for developers and should not generally be ran.

`pytest -n auto tests`
`pytest -v -n auto tests`
